d 'APPLYVARLABELS': module to apply variable labels to the data in memory from a two-column (Variable, Label) crosswalk
d
d  Label the variables in memory from an Excel workbook or a
d delimited file that lists each variable name beside the label it
d should carry. Solves the Statalist problem (thread 1768839) where
d a levelsof/tokenize loop puts the wrong label on the wrong
d variable because levelsof sorts the labels alphabetically.
d applyvarlabels reads the crosswalk in row order and matches every
d label to its variable BY NAME, never by position. It writes a
d capture-guarded relabel do-file (a variable named in the
d crosswalk but absent from the data is skipped, not an error),
d runs it to apply the labels, and prints an inventory of what did
d not line up: crosswalk rows with no such variable, and variables
d in memory with no crosswalk row. The data in memory are never
d sorted, dropped, or reordered - the crosswalk is read in its own
d frame, so nothing changes but the variable labels themselves. The
d generated do-file is a keepable, rerunnable artifact (see
d dofile()). Reads .xlsx/.xls and .csv/.tsv/.txt; nocase matches
d names ignoring case; norun writes the relabel do-file without
d applying it. 
d
d KW: variable labels; codebook; data management; Excel
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f applyvarlabels.ado
f applyvarlabels.sthlp
f ../e/example_applyvarlabels.do
f ../e/example_varlabels.xlsx
f ../m/make_example_varlabels.py
